diff --git a/features/adding-todos.feature b/features/adding-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e96b327
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/adding-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Adding todos
+  As a user
+  I want to enter a new todo in the input field
+  So that I can track things I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Enter creates a todo from the input text
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains a todo with title "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: The input field is cleared after adding a todo
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the new todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: Empty input is ignored
+    When the user presses Enter on an empty new todo input
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only input is ignored
+    When the user types "   " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Input is trimmed before creating a todo
+    When the user types "  Buy groceries  " in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains a todo with title "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: New todos are appended in order
+    When the user types "First" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user types "Second" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 2 todos
+    And the first todo has title "First"
+    And the second todo has title "Second"
+
+  Scenario: The new todo input is focused on page load
+    Then the new todo input is focused
diff --git a/features/clearing-completed.feature b/features/clearing-completed.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5538813
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/clearing-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+Feature: Clearing completed todos
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos at once
+  So that I can clean up my list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button removes completed todos
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 todos
+    And the todo list contains a todo with title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed does not remove active todos
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no todos are completed
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when at least one todo is completed
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is visible
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all unchecked state resets after clearing completed
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles all todos on
+    And the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the todo list is empty
diff --git a/features/displaying-todos.feature b/features/displaying-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ac5d741
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/displaying-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Feature: Displaying todos
+  As a user
+  I want to see my todo list and the app sections appear and disappear appropriately
+  So that I have a clear view of what I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Main section and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Main section and footer appear after adding a todo
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
+
+  Scenario: Main section and footer disappear after removing the last todo
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    And the user removes the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Each todo shows a checkbox, label, and destroy button
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" has a toggle checkbox
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" has a label with text "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" has a destroy button
+
+  Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox is present
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is visible
diff --git a/features/editing-todos.feature b/features/editing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6eb758b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user
+  I want to double-click a todo to edit its title
+  So that I can correct or update my todos
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo activates editing mode
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    And the edit input for "Buy groceries" is focused
+
+  Scenario: The edit input contains the current todo title
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the edit input for "Buy groceries" has value "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edit
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input for "Buy groceries" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains a todo with title "Buy organic groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy organic groceries" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Blurring the edit input saves the edit
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input for "Buy groceries" and blurs
+    Then the todo list contains a todo with title "Buy organic groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Escape discards the edit
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input for "Buy groceries" and presses Escape
+    Then the todo list contains a todo with title "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Saving an empty edit removes the todo
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user clears the edit input for "Buy groceries" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Saving whitespace-only edit removes the todo
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "   " in the edit input for "Buy groceries" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Edit input is trimmed before saving
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "  Buy organic groceries  " in the edit input for "Buy groceries" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains a todo with title "Buy organic groceries"
diff --git a/features/item-count.feature b/features/item-count.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1101f48
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/item-count.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+Feature: Item count
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many active todos remain
+  So that I know how much work is left
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Shows "0 items left" when there are no todos
+    Then the item count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Shows "1 item left" with one active todo
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the item count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Shows correct count with multiple active todos
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user adds a todo "Do laundry"
+    Then the item count shows "3 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Completed todos are not counted
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the item count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: All completed shows "0 items left"
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the item count shows "0 items left"
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9ac6307
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my data
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Todos survive a page reload
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 2 todos
+    And the todo list contains a todo with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo list contains a todo with title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Todo completion state survives a page reload
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+
+  Scenario: Item count persists across reload
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the item count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Todos are stored with correct shape in localStorage
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then localStorage "todos-vanillajs" contains an array with 1 items
+    And the stored todo at index 0 has title "Buy groceries" and completed false
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ca78faa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todos by status using URL hash
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: All filter is selected by default
+    Then the "All" filter link is selected
+    And the "Active" filter link is not selected
+    And the "Completed" filter link is not selected
+
+  Scenario: Navigating to #/active shows only active todos
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user navigates to the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+    And the "Active" filter link is selected
+    And the "All" filter link is not selected
+
+  Scenario: Navigating to #/completed shows only completed todos
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user navigates to the "Completed" filter
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is not visible
+    And the "Completed" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Navigating to #/ shows all todos
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user navigates to the "Completed" filter
+    And the user navigates to the "All" filter
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across page reload
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user navigates to the "Active" filter
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is visible
diff --git a/features/toggling-todos.feature b/features/toggling-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d809fe3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggling-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+Feature: Toggling todos
+  As a user
+  I want to mark individual todos as complete or active
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clicking a todo's checkbox marks it as completed
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+
+  Scenario: Clicking a completed todo's checkbox marks it as active
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Completed todo gets the completed class on its parent li
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo element "Buy groceries" has the class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all marks all todos as completed
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles all todos on
+    Then all todos are completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all marks all todos as active when toggled off
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles all todos on
+    And the user toggles all todos off
+    Then all todos are not completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all becomes checked when all individual todos are checked
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all becomes unchecked when at least one todo is unchecked
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles all todos on
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Completed todos are hidden when viewing Active filter
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user navigates to the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is not visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Active todos are hidden when viewing Completed filter
+    When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user navigates to the "Completed" filter
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" is visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is not visible
